# PLAN3_DE2 — CLI main TimeCap and bench help

File: openOODA/audit/plan3_de2.oot
Wave 1 WRITE. Own cli/main.oo only. No cmd_more.oo. No oodac/runtime/std. No dirty parent.

Logline: Product CLI main now takes TimeCap and forwards it to bench. Help names the real command.
Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-bench` file `cli/main.oo`. Limit 256 lines.
Beats:
  1. Add time: &TimeCap to pub fn main.
  2. Pass time on the bench dispatch line.
  3. Replace the bare bench help mention. Record the line count.

## 1. Signature

```
pub fn main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String])
```

Wave 0 RT already proved the seed accepts this shape. Parameter name is `time`.
No date. No shell timer. Other command dispatch is unchanged.

## 2. Bench dispatch

```
if cmd == "bench" { run_ooda_bench(fs, sys, time, args); return; }
```

DE1 owns the four-arg body in cmd_more.oo. This file only writes the call.
If cmd_more still has the three-arg stub, HYG/INT rebuild after both land.

## 3. Help

Kept emit-health and errdigest. Removed the grouped ` | bench` floor.
Added one line:

```
  ooda bench <file.oo> [--run]        # time oodac check
```

print_help stayed in cli/main.oo. No cli/cli_help.oo split.

